+      DECLARED flag family as a whole token (vLLM ``--chat-template`` vs
+      llama.cpp ``--chat-template-file``; a prefix of the other never
+      counts) naming the mounted path, same line or adjacent list item —
+      UNLESS the mount alone is load-bearing: the template is mounted
+      OVER the model dir's own ``chat_template.jinja`` and the engine
+      auto-loads it (carnice is ``wired_at: [volumes]``; qwen38 declares
+      ``flag_required: false`` — SGLang needs no flag, and the vLLM flag
+      is only the Anthropic-router hint, vllm#58754). A flag that IS
+      present must still name the mounted path — a flag pointing at
+      another template means the engine renders the OTHER one, so the
+      mount is not in use.
+    """
+    spec = patch.get("delivery_spec") or {}
+    mounted_at = spec.get("mounted_at")
+    if not mounted_at:
+        return False
+    sources = _chat_template_sources(patch)
+    if not sources:
+        return False
